    id: "what-is-patience", number: "01", question: "What is patience actually made of?", title: "Find the war and the two motives",
    description: "Take patience apart into knowledge, state and act, see why it belongs to human beings alone, and get the definition the rest of the book runs on. Then follow Ghazali into the strangest passage in the book, where the two angels who write your deeds turn out to keep their pages somewhere you cannot look.",
    payoff: "You stop confusing composure with patience, and you can say exactly what is holding.",
